## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design policy-grounded assistants with explainable outputs and integrated escalation.

## Key Concepts
- Grounding with Cognitive Search embeddings
- Confidence scoring and provenance tracking
- Safe escalation to ticketing (ServiceNow)
- Data lineage and logging for audits

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudocode: compute final answer with grounding and provenance
async function answer(query) {
  const docs = await searchKB(query);
  const prompt = buildPrompt(query, docs);
  const res = await openai.complete({ prompt });
  const provenance = docs.map(d => d.id);
  const confidence = res.meta?.confidence ?? 0.9;
  if (confidence < 0.8) await ticketSystem.create('Review needed', { query, provenance });
  return { text: res.text, confidence, provenance };
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you handle KB versioning and rollback?
- How would you validate calibration of confidence scores in production?

## Why This Is Asked

Assesses ability to design end-to-end Azure OpenAI-powered data-governance tooling that handles multi-tenant isolation, secure KB grounding, and robust testing.

## Key Concepts
- Data lineage ingestion and normalization across Synapse/Data Factory.
- Versioned KB in Azure Blob and Cognitive Search integration.
- Per-tenant isolation with Key Vault-backed Cosmos DB storage.
- Prompt engineering with fallback chains and confidence scoring.
- Data redaction and auditability.

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-code for gap-filling using KB
async function fillLineageGap(partialLineage, kbClient) {
  if (partialLineage.isComplete()) return partialLineage;
  const kb = await kbClient.query(partialLineage.pattern);
  return partialLineage.enrich(kb);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you measure the accuracy of enrichment?
- How would you handle cycles or conflicting KB results?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to architect a multi-tenant Azure OpenAI flow integrated with DevOps, covering data lineage, security, and performance.

## Key Concepts
- Azure OpenAI + API Management
- Cognitive Search KB in Blob
- Per-tenant RBAC (Azure AD)
- PII redaction (Text Analytics)
- Data Lake logging
- Canary deployments and end-to-end latency goals

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo orchestration snippet showing tenant context, diff->prompt, and moderation
async function reviewPR(prDiff, tenantId){
  const kb = await loadKB(tenantId);
  const prompt = buildPrompt(prDiff, kb, tenantId);
  const review = await openAiReview(prompt);
  if(hasPIIRisk(review)){ redact(review); }
  await storeLogs(tenantId, {prDiff, review});
  return review.comments;
}
``` 

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you validate and monitor prompt drift across tenants without leaking data?
- What latency and cost controls would you put in place for high-velocity repos?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests multilingual orchestration, privacy, and end-to-end data flow in Azure OpenAI pipelines.

## Key Concepts
- Azure Translator Text API
- Azure Cognitive Search over Blob KB
- Text Analytics for PII redaction
- Cosmos DB per-tenant language settings
- Durable Functions orchestration
- API Management as a gateway

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo code for flow
async function handleQuery(userQuery, tenantId) {
  const lang = await getTenantLang(tenantId);
  const enQuery = await translateToEnglish(userQuery, lang);
  const answer = await groundKB(enQuery);
  const redacted = redactPII(answer, enQuery);
  return await translateFromEnglish(redacted, lang);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test translation fidelity and PII redaction in CI?
- How would you monitor latency across translation, search, and OpenAI calls?

## Why This Is Asked
This tests practical security-first design for Azure OpenAI with code-gen, focusing on secret redaction, key vault integration, tenant isolation, and auditable logging.

## Key Concepts
- Secret management with Azure Key Vault and Managed Identity
- Request/response redaction and policy enforcement
- Data isolation per tenant and private networking
- End-to-end auditing in Purview
- Testing: redaction fuzzing and integration tests

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo: redact secrets before sending to OpenAI
function redact(input, keys){
  let out = input;
  keys.forEach(k => { out = out.replace(new RegExp(k, 'g'), 'REDACTED'); });
  return out;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test drift in redaction rules across tenants?
- What data plane logs would you guard and what retention policy would you apply?
